invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: widemul_poly1305_avx2 reads CH_CPU_AVX2 alone, so a session that
  states AVX2 and not the multiply bit runs the kernel, whose VPMULUDQ
  no statement covers, and the native copy's update under the
  decomposition's answer. The bytes are the same. bin/x86_kernels_test
  counts the kernel's calls under every ch_cfg.cpu value, and the script
  builds it for x86-64, where widemul.h compiles the function.

--- old
    return widemul_native(widemul) && (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    (void)widemul;
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
